<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 23 September, from 63 BCE to 1939.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rome" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/63-bce">63 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,088 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The future Emperor Augustus is born in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gaius Octavius was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, great-nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. As Augustus he ended the civil wars and turned the Republic into a monarchy that lasted for centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1122">1122 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">904 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Callixtus II and Henry V agree the Concordat of Worms</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Worms, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-callixtus-ii">Pope Callixtus II</a> and Emperor Henry V ended the Investiture Controversy. The emperor gave up investing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> with ring and staff, while in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> elections were held in his presence and he granted the elected bishop the regalia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concordat-of-worms">Concordat of Worms</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-callixtus-ii">Pope Callixtus II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-holy-roman-emperor">Henry V, Holy Roman Emperor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1338 CE <span class="tih-ago">688 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The French defeat the English at the Battle of Arnemuiden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, a French force defeated the English in the war's first naval battle. It was the first recorded European naval battle using artillery: the English ship Christopher carried three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannons</a> and one handgun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1459 CE <span class="tih-ago">567 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Yorkists win the Battle of Blore Heath</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Blore Heath in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staffordshire">Staffordshire</a>, near Market Drayton, the Yorkists won a battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>, the struggle between the houses of Lancaster and York for the English throne that lasted until 1487.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1642">1642 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">384 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Royalists win the skirmish at Powick Bridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the first engagement between the principal field armies of the Royalists and Parliamentarians, Prince Rupert's Royalist force defeated a Parliamentarian detachment under Colonel John Brown south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcester">Worcester</a>. Brown had been sent to capture a Royalist convoy of valuables.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1779">1779 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">247 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Paul Jones captures HMS Serapis off Flamborough Head</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a brutal moonlit battle, John Paul Jones's sinking Bonhomme Richard captured HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serapis">Serapis</a> off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire">Yorkshire</a>. His later-reported reply 'I have not yet begun to fight' became a naval legend.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1846">1846 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Johann Galle discovers Neptune</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> Observatory, Johann <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galle">Galle</a> found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neptune">Neptune</a> within a degree of where Urbain Le Verrier had calculated. It was the first planet found by mathematical prediction.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sigmund Freud dies in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigmund-freud">Freud</a>, who had fled Nazi-occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> the year before, died aged 83 after his doctor gave him lethal doses of morphine at his request. His theories of the unconscious reshaped twentieth-century thought.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigmund-freud">Sigmund Freud</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 23 September <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-dudley"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-dudley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph Dudley</span><span class="tp">1647–1720</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-bosch"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-bosch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Bosch</span><span class="tp">1861–1942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-joaquin-chamorro-cardenal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-joaquin-chamorro-cardenal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro Joaquín Chamorro Cardenal</span><span class="tp">1924–1978</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 23 September <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/snorri-sturluson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Snorri Sturluson</span><span class="tp">1179–1241</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/beatrice-of-provence"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/beatrice-of-provence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Beatrice of Provence</span><span class="tp">c. 1229–1267</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-prince-of-viana"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-prince-of-viana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles, Prince of Viana</span><span class="tp">1421–1461</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/azai-hisamasa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azai-hisamasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Azai Hisamasa</span><span class="tp">1526–1573</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christian-thomasius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christian-thomasius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christian Thomasius</span><span class="tp">1655–1728</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/herman-boerhaave"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herman-boerhaave.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Herman Boerhaave</span><span class="tp">1668–1738</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-gervasio-artigas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Gervasio Artigas</span><span class="tp">1764–1850</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-joseph-papineau"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-joseph-papineau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis-Joseph Papineau</span><span class="tp">1786–1871</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pablo-neruda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pablo-neruda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pablo Neruda</span><span class="tp">1904–1973</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
